JDK AND COMPILING CODE:
-> jdk (java development kit) is used to compile our whatever written java code.
-> and it's a kit which will be installed by developers in their systems inorder to compile the java code.
-> JVM and JRE are the part of the this ENTIRE JDKit.
UNDERSTANDING THE JVM :
-> jvm (java virtual machiene) is where after compilation it runs to convert byte code into executable runable code in java.
-> jvm is part of JRE.
ROLE OF JRE:
-> JRE (java runtime environment) creates a runtime environment where it has multiful external files or frameworks or
   whatever resources and it has JVM as its part where the files in jvm need some external files and those will be 
   provided by this Java runtime environment for successfully run the code in java.
RELATIONSHIP BTW JDK AND JRE:
-> the JDK is the first block where it has the second layer
   as JRE and the third layer inside the JRE as the JVM.
